
  <sn><md>### Venn-diagram

![img](https://images.twinkl.co.uk/tw1n/image/private/t_630_eco/image_repo/63/cf/T2-M-261-Venn-Diagram-Template-1_ver_1.jpg)

* **Creator:** **[John Venn](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d7/John_Venn_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=original) (1834–1883)** introduced the method of `representing sets using diagrams`.

* **Name:** These visual representations are named **Venn diagrams** in his honor.
* In a Venn diagram, geometric shapes are typically used to represent different sets:
* **Rectangular Regions:** Generally used to represent the **Universal Set ($U$)**.
* **Circular Regions:** Generally used to represent subsets within the universal set (e.g., set $A$, set $B$).
</md></sn>
