<sn><md>### Common Venn Diagram Types Shown

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
1. **Universal Set ($U$):**
Represented by a shaded rectangular region.

2. **Intersection of Sets ($A \cap B$):**
Represented by two overlapping circles where only the overlapping middle region is shaded.

3. **Union of Sets ($A \cup B$):**
Represented by two overlapping circles where both complete circular regions are shaded together.
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
![img](https://statisticseasily.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/The-Union-and-Intersection-of-Two-Sets-3-1024x576.jpg)
:::
:::

Purpose &amp; Application
By using Venn diagrams, the **properties of sets** and **operations on sets** can be easily determined and visually understood.
